From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niklas Sheth <hi@niklassheth.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 17:06:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] drm/asahi: G16: give each VM its own compute scratch pool

The compute FList (16 operand buffers of 2 MiB plus its 96 KiB ring
directory) was one device-wide pool: the opening client's pages, mapped
read-write at fixed VAs into every VM's compute root, with one support
object and hardware FList slot 2. Shader private memory does not go
through a separate permission check: any client could load and store
those pages through a forged pointer. From a separate Vulkan process,
99-100% of the words of another process's compute buffers were its
scratch markers, during its dispatches and after it exited. The pages
keep the last user's data, and the directory is writable as well, so a
client could also corrupt other clients' live scratch or redirect their
private memory and fault the GPU. This is the LeftoverLocals class of
leak (CVE-2023-4969). Metal gives each process its own pool.

Give each VM's compute root a private pool at the same VAs, allocated
at that VM's first compute command and charged to the submitting
client's memory cgroup (GFP_KERNEL_ACCOUNT, as the render pool). The
pages are owned by the compute root, so fdinfo reports them, and are
freed with the root once its last Work retires. Each pool gets its own
support object, shared state page and hardware slot from the render
support leases (slots 3..59), so no two pools in use share a slot; the
compute root retains the lease, and pending or quarantined Works retain
the root. The support's shared state now counts the Works submitted
against that support, as for render, instead of the device-wide compute
publication count. VMs that never run compute pay nothing; one that
does pays 32.1 MiB.

ENOMEM and ENOSPC (no free support lease) while setting up the pool no
longer quarantine the VM: pages already allocated are kept and a retry
resumes.

Two research knobs, read at each VM's first compute (module parameters,
and debugfs asahi_m4/<name> at runtime):
- compute_pool_buffers: buffers per private pool, 1..=16 (default 16,
  the size of the former device-wide pool).
- compute_shares_render_pool (experimental, default 0): run compute on
  the VM's render pool and support instead, mapping its directory,
  descriptor table and buffers into the compute root at the same VAs
  (allocating them first if the VM has not rendered). This costs no
  memory or lease, but one FList slot then serves the TA, 3D and CDM
  engines of the VM at once.
